{{also|TUR|Tur|tur|tür|tùr|Túr|túr|tűr}}
==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|de|Thür|Thüre||obsolete}}
* {{alter|de|Türe||dated, regional}}

===Etymology===
{{root|de|ine-pro|*dʰwer-}} {{dercat|de|gem-pro|ine-pro|inh=1}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|-}}, from {{inh|de|goh|turi}}, from {{der|de|gem-pro|*dur}}. Compare {{cog|en|door}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/tyːr/|/tyːɐ̯/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Tür.OGG|audio}}
* {{rhymes|de|yːɐ̯|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Türen|Türchen|dim2=Türlein}}

# [[door]] {{gloss|rigid plane on a hinge}}
#: {{uxi|de|Die '''Tür''' ist aus Eichenholz.|The '''door''' is made of oak wood.}}
#: {{uxi|de|Kannst du bitte die '''Tür''' zumachen?!|Can you please shut the '''door'''?!}}
#: {{uxi|de|Hast du schon an die '''Tür''' geklopft.|Have you knocked on the '''door''' yet?}}
#: {{uxi|de|Plötzlich klopfte es an der (also: die) '''Tür'''.|Suddenly someone knocked at the '''door'''.}}
# [[door]]; [[doorway]] {{gloss|passage that can be blocked with such a plane}}
#: {{uxi|de|Er stand in der '''Tür'''.|He was standing in the '''door[way]'''.}}

